Potion Throwing Effects:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
In addition to quaffing potions, they can also be potent weapons when thrown
at a monster in such a way as to shatter them.  This section describes the
effects that the various potions will have when smashed over the head (or
other body part) of menacing creatures.  Note that while monsters can now
throw potions at you, you will suffer vapor effect of the potion (see Potion
Vapor Effects).  These effects are for monsters only, and are described as
follows:

Potion name
  (Cur)  This will describe the effects that will occur when a monster is hit
         by a cursed variety of this potion.  If this section is missing, the
         effects are the same as for the regular potion.
         Message: "This is the message the game will give you."
         Hallucinating: "You may also see different messages under certain
         conditions."
  (Reg)  This describes the effect that the standard potion will have (i.e.
         non-cursed and non-blessed).
         Message: "This is the message the game will give you."
         Hallucinating: "You may also see different messages under certain
         conditions."
  (Bls)  This will describe the effects that will occur when a monster is hit
         by a blessed variety of this potion.  If this section is missing,
         the effects are the same as for the regular potion.
         Message: "This is the message the game will give you."
         Hallucinating: "You may also see different messages under certain
         conditions."

Notes:  If you hit a monster with a potion, there is a 20% chance that you
will do 1 point of damage to the monster, if it currently has more than one
hit point.

Also, monsters have a percentage chance of resisting ill effects that is equal
to their level plus their magic resistance plus five.  In other words, a sixth
level monster with a 10% magic resistance would have a 21% chance of resisting
ill effects from being hit by a potion.

Blindness
  (Reg)  The monster will be blinded for 64-96 turns regardless of whether it
         resists or not, and 0-32 turns more if it does not resist.
         Message:  None
Booze
  (Reg)  If the monster does not resist, it becomes confused.
         Message:  None
Confusion
  (Reg)  If the monster does not resist, it becomes confused.
         Message:  None
Extra healing
  (Reg)  The monster hit is healed up to maximum hit points.
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks sound and hale again."
         Blind:  No message
Gain ability
  (Reg)  The monster hit is healed up to maximum hit points.
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks sound and hale again."
         Blind:  No message
Healing
  (Reg)  The monster hit is healed up to maximum hit points.
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks sound and hale again."
         Blind:  No message
Invisibility
  (Reg)  The monster hit becomes invisible.
         Message:  None
Paralysis
  (Reg)  The monster hit becomes paralyzed for 1-25 turns (no chance of
         resisting).
         Message:  None
Restore ability
  (Reg)  The monster hit is healed up to maximum hit points.
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks sound and hale again."
         Blind:  No message
Sickness
  (Reg)  If the monster does not resist, the following effects occur:  If the
         monster's hit point max is greater than three, its hit point max is
         halved.  If the monster's hit points are greater than two, its hit
         points are halved.  (Hit points cannot be more than hit point max.)
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks rather ill."
         Blind:  No message
Speed
  (Reg)  Slow monsters hit become normal, while normal monsters become fast
Water
  (Cur)  Cursed potions of water are unholy water.
         If the monster hit is undead of a demon, it will be healed 2-12 hit
         points.
         Message:  "The [monster name] looks healthier."
         If the monster hit is a gremlin, it will multiply.
         Message:  "The gremlin multiplies."
  (Reg)  Regular potions of water can be water or impure water.
         If the monster hit is a gremlin, it will multiply.
         Message:  "The gremlin multiplies."
  (Bls)  Blessed potions of water are holy water.
         If the monster hit is undead or a demon, it will take 2-12 points of
         damage.
         Message:  "The [monster name] shrieks in pain!"
         If the monster hit is a gremlin, it will multiply.
         Message:  "The gremlin multiplies."

